notes               = "Untitled in source. Whether دیوار زندانم is a literal prison wall or a figure for where the poet finds himself in ۱۳۶۸ is not settled by the page, and is left open here rather than decided. The turn is that a shadow — the thing a wall casts, and the thing least able to pass through one — is what makes the wall kinder. ۱۳۶۸/۹/۷ is 7 Azar, an autumn month, so the Gregorian half is 1989 (+621). Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

نَه...
تو را به من راه نمی‌دهند...
یک روزِ آفتابی
پشتِ دیوار زندانم بیا...
سایهٔ تو...
دیوار را مهربان‌تر می‌کند.
۱۳۶۸/۹/۷

===machine===

No...
They will not let you through to me...
Some sunny day
come to the far side of my prison wall...
Your shadow...
makes the wall kinder.
1368/9/7

===lantern===

No...
they will not let you through to me...
Some sunny day
come to the far side of my prison wall...
Your shadow
makes the wall kinder.

1368/9/7

